%N A399712 a(n) = the index m such that A398414(m) = prime(n). If prime(n) never occurs in A398414, then a(n) = -1.
%C A399712 Most likely all prime numbers appear in A398414, so all numbers appear in this sequence.
%H A399712 Michel Marcus, <a href="/A399712/b399712.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..2878</a>
%e A399712 Since prime(4) = 7 and A398414(9) = 7, a(4) = 9.
%o A399712 (PARI) findp(n, va) = for (i=1, #va, if (va[i] == prime(n), return(i)));
%o A399712 listp(nn) = my(va=lista(nn), list=List()); for (n=1, nn, my(i=findp(n, va)); if (i, listput(list, i), break)); Vec(list); \\ where lista comes from A398414; _Michel Marcus_, Sep 14 2026
%Y A399712 Cf. A398414, A397866, A397866.
